{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":20,"code":"PRO","name":"Proverbs","testament":"OT"},"chapter":9,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"PRO 9:1"},"Wisdom hath builded her house, she hath hewn out her seven pillars: ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 9:1"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"PRO 9:2"},"She hath killed her beasts; she hath mingled her wine; she hath also furnished her table. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 9:2"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"PRO 9:3"},"She hath sent forth her maidens: she crieth upon the highest places of the city, ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 9:3"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"PRO 9:4"},"Whoso ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," simple, let him turn in hither: ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["as for "]},"him that wanteth understanding, she saith to him, ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 9:4"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"PRO 9:5"},"Come, eat of my bread, and drink of the wine ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["which"]}," I have mingled. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 9:5"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"PRO 9:6"},"Forsake the foolish, and live; and go in the way of understanding. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 9:6"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"PRO 9:7"},"He that reproveth a scorner getteth to himself shame: and he that rebuketh a wicked ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["man getteth"]}," himself a blot. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 9:7"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"PRO 9:8"},"Reprove not a scorner, lest he hate thee: rebuke a wise man, and he will love thee. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 9:8"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"PRO 9:9"},"Give ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["instruction"]}," to a wise ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["man,"]}," and he will be yet wiser: teach a just ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["man,"]}," and he will increase in learning. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 9:9"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"PRO 9:10"},"The fear of the LORD ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," the beginning of wisdom: and the knowledge of the holy ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," understanding. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 9:10"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"PRO 9:11"},"For by me thy days shall be multiplied, and the years of thy life shall be increased. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 9:11"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"PRO 9:12"},"If thou be wise, thou shalt be wise for thyself: but ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["if"]}," thou scornest, thou alone shalt bear ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["it."]},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 9:12"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"PRO 9:13"},"A foolish woman ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," clamorous: ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["she is"]}," simple, and knoweth nothing. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 9:13"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"14","sid":"PRO 9:14"},"For she sitteth at the door of her house, on a seat in the high places of the city, ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 9:14"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"15","sid":"PRO 9:15"},"To call passengers who go right on their ways: ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 9:15"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"16","sid":"PRO 9:16"},"Whoso ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," simple, let him turn in hither: and ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["as for "]},"him that wanteth understanding, she saith to him, ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 9:16"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"17","sid":"PRO 9:17"},"Stolen waters are sweet, and bread ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["eaten"]}," in secret is pleasant. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 9:17"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"18","sid":"PRO 9:18"},"But he knoweth not that the dead ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," there; ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and that "]},"her guests ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," in the depths of hell. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 9:18"}]}]}
